From 388e81fb72cdf4b7e001598f4dce9c4089ec2dcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:35:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): preserve authoritative check ordering across
 remote claims [daveey]

Why: the quota fence folded losing tied successes, and absence from a local snapshot could not order unsynced remote claims. Select per-second winning receipts and use consistent UUIDv7 claim-initiation milliseconds as additional bounded clock evidence. No distributed clock-skew guarantee.

Proof: tied-result and actual in-memory Board pre-recovery remote-claim tests fail before and pass after. Nine race mutants killed. Focused/scanner suites:1494 pass. Prior unchanged broad Kanban suite:789 files,14474 pass,24 skip. Non-executable profile-home checker executed. Historical replay remains counterfactual, not natural proof.
